# `docs/raw/` — the raw-source dropzone (immutable)

Drop sources here **verbatim**: articles, notes, transcripts, clippings, exported
threads — anything you want turned into knowledge. One rule:

> **Nothing here is ever edited — not by the CLI, not by the LLM.** Raw sources
> are immutable input. You only ever *add* files.

The `wiki` skill's **Ingest** workflow reads what you drop here and writes
structured, interlinked pages under `docs/wiki/pages/`, recording provenance with
a `sources:` frontmatter entry pointing back at the raw file. Until a page derives
from a raw file, `csdd wiki lint` flags it as an **unprocessed source** — so
nothing you drop is silently forgotten.

The graph indexes each file here as an opaque `raw_source` node (path only; the
content is never parsed). Its purpose in the graph is provenance (`derived_from`
targets) and the unprocessed-source lint.

## Dropping a repository

Source code is a different kind of drop: a repository is not something to ingest
page by page, it is something to **read**. Put the checkout here as a directory
(or a `.zip`/`.tar.gz` you unpack beside itself) and run **`/csdd-codewiki`**. It
compiles the whole repo into one cited wiki document —
`docs/raw/<owner>-<repo>.md` — where every claim cites a real file and line
range, verified by `csdd codewiki lint`. *That* document is the source you then
ingest with `/csdd-wiki-ingest`.

```
docs/raw/
├── widget/            ← the checkout: material, never indexed, never edited
├── widget.zip         ← the archive it came from: material once unpacked
└── acme-widget.md     ← the codewiki document: the source that gets ingested
```

A directory carrying a `.git/` or a dependency manifest (`go.mod`,
`package.json`, `pyproject.toml`, `Cargo.toml`, …) is recognized as a checkout
and left out of the graph entirely. Otherwise a 200-file repository would become
200 `raw_source` nodes and 200 unprocessed-source findings, and the lint that is
supposed to tell you "you dropped something and forgot it" would be permanently
red. The obligation is not lost — it moves to the one document derived from the
checkout. An archive nobody unpacked stays flagged, exactly as it should.
